---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
---
<Page
  title="Due diligence firms"
  description="ArborSpace for technical due diligence firms: connect the seller's documents, apply your senior engineers' checks and give lenders conclusions they can trace."
  eyebrow="Customers · Due diligence firms"
  heading="Independent engineers, working for lenders."
  lead="A due diligence firm is paid for the judgement of its senior engineers. ArborSpace connects the seller’s documents in one model, applies the checks those engineers always make, and submits every conclusion to the engineer in charge."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What the firm faces</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>A data room</strong> of maintenance plans, manufacturer documentation, asset registers and financial models.</li>
          <li><strong>Lenders</strong> who want to know what each finding means for debt repayment.</li>
          <li><strong>Senior judgement</strong> that is applied engagement after engagement, but rarely written down.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What ArborSpace brings</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>One model</strong> linking the plan, the equipment, the history and the financial model.</li>
          <li><strong>Readable rules</strong> for the checks your senior engineers make.</li>
          <li><strong>A review queue</strong> where the engineer in charge approves or rejects each finding.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Worked example</p>
        <h2>Alder Creek, a 612 MW combined-cycle plant.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          See how the ontology connects a maintenance plan to its effect on the debt, and how four
          actors get four answers from the same model.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/solutions/energy-assets">See the Energy Assets example</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
